 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "A leaf for wealth that will not avail, wind for the frosty blast of the parable (no crop destroyed on screen), a lamp for the signs made clear. Nothing for the Fire. No motif on the negated «لا تتخذوا بطانة». STAGING v4: 116-117: the disbelievers (d) stand by their wheat fields at dusk; leaf plate for the wealth that will not avail (children not drawn); nothing for the Fire. The parable: gusts of wind on «ريح» and «أصابت» (wind plate), no crop destroyed on screen and no storm event on people; they wring their hands on 117:18 (As-Sa'di: nothing but toil and more regret). 118: the believers shake their heads on «تتخذوا» (they do not take them as intimates); the enemies (e) speak on «بدت» (hatred from their mouths) and turn on «تخفي» (what they hide); the camera moves to the believers on 118:24 and the lamp on «الآيات» stands over them."
 },
